Legend (canonical)

Downward solid arrows = intent/control routing through Engine into agents. 

Upward dotted arrows = telemetry, metrics, and evidence returning to human + governance. 

Governance arrows into E = pre-flight constraint supremacy and runtime safe-mode/demotion gates. 


Narrative walkthrough (Appendix-L style)

1. Intent intake. H provides I₀, initial constraints C₀, and budget B. Intent is normalized to I′ (Engine is not allowed to originate goals). 


2. Governed consolidation. GK compiles policy into C and sets risk class ceilings for AB/RB. Plans violating C are rejected pre-flight. 


3. Task graph synthesis. E expands I′ into TG with dependencies and candidate bands. 


4. Economic admissibility. EC prices TG vs B; over-budget plans are optimized or returned for override. 


5. RB/AB gating. E computes RB per node and selects admissible AB state. Any RB crossing requires human authorization. 


6. Dry-run preview (if high autonomy / RB-prox). E generates a no-side-effect plan preview and requests H pre-approval.


7. Contracted dispatch. TG nodes are bound into MCP contracts and delegated to agents with explicit ceilings. 


8. Execution + telemetry. Agents execute, returning outputs, confidence, realized cost, and safety signals. 


9. Metrics + lineage. E updates SI/HSS/SCP, commits an immutable lineage hash, and reports evidence to governance.
